# XIII. The Four-Year Reform Program

The first four years should focus on establishing the infrastructure of renewal.

## Year 1 — Establish

* conservation performance standard;
* capacity assessment;
* data inventory;
* early-warning pilots;
* funding-alignment review;
* evaluation capacity;
* initial dashboard;
* priority ecological pilots.

## Year 2 — Institutionalize

* expand performance standards;
* formalize data standards;
* establish ecological-scale partnerships;
* integrate workforce findings into planning;
* establish restoration lifecycle reporting;
* expand early-warning systems.

## Year 3 — Scale

* expand successful pilots;
* strengthen ecological-scale coordination;
* expand interoperable datasets;
* improve assessment capacity;
* scale workforce initiatives;
* redirect resources toward demonstrated bottlenecks.

## Year 4 — Evaluate

Classify major reforms:

**Continue → Modify → Scale → End**

The objective is to institutionalize what works rather than preserve reforms merely because they were created.

