# XVI. What the Strategy Does Not Attempt to Do

American Conservation Renewal is not:

* a proposal to federalize all conservation;
* a proposal to eliminate state authority;
* a proposal to diminish Tribal sovereignty;
* a universal land-management prescription;
* a single climate policy;
* a restoration-only strategy;
* a proposal to maximize conservation spending;
* a proposal to maximize regulation;
* a technology strategy;
* a single national ecological score;
* a replacement for existing conservation laws;
* a replacement for scientific judgment;
* a prediction of specific ecological conditions in 2050.

It is a **systems strategy**.

